  "description": "Discontinued. The Soul legacy continues in the Solaris (effectively the Soul in 29\" format) and the BFe (for when you need a bit more than the Soul). This page is kept as an archive record for owners and for anyone researching an older Cotic Soul.\n\nThe Cotic Soul was our iconic light and lively trail blazer. Slim, subtle, tough and beautiful: the ultimate expression of a steel hardtail.\n\nThe Soul is the founding model of the Cotic range, conceived in 2003 as a modern steel hardtail. We wanted the best frame we could make, something no one else was making back then. It was super progressive and quickly became an icon, winning multiple tests and awards over the following years. It spawned many imitators, but the Soul was the original, the template.\n\nThe 5th and final generation Soul captured that progressive spirit. Tough, light, fun, interactive, comfortable, but at heart a singletrack scalpel. It was optimised around 120mm forks with the strength for up to 140mm, and the Reynolds 853 tubeset had our famously subtle, traction-rich feel. We bombed down Pyrenean mountains, battered across British hills, whizzed between the trees and strapped bags on for nights out in the hills.\n\nFinishes: Blue with Magenta, Orange with Blue, and Mercury with Orange.",
